I wrote the plan to session_plan/, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the git add failed. The files are on disk: task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md. Whatever reads them next has to read them from disk, or the commit needs git add -f.

Task 1 (evolve): make room under `src/prompt.rs`'s size limit. The file is 4006 lines against a recorded 3913, so it is 93 into a 100-line grace band. Seven more lines would fail the size test, and the next fix to --print would hit that. The task moves the helpers that prepend notes to each turn (the effort hint and the "external server failed to connect" note), with their tests, into a new child module src/prompt/turn_prefix.rs. It then records the new line count in tests/module_size.rs. The task asks for the test count before and after, and they must be equal. No call sites change.

Task 2 (product): tell stream-json consumers when a configured server failed to connect. Planning turned up something the assessment didn't know:
• **Already covered:** the --output-format json envelope already reports failed MCP/OpenAPI servers in its external_servers field (#895).
• **Not covered:** the stream-json path has no startup event at all. It only forwards the agent library's own events, and a test pins `agentStart` as the first one. So a stream-json consumer has no machine-readable way to learn a server failed.

The task adds one {"type":"externalServers", …} line after the final event, only when at least one server failed. It reuses the envelope's existing serializer, and healthy runs stay byte-identical. It must run after Task 1, because it needs the headroom in prompt.rs. It includes a clause saying what to report if stream-json turns out to already surface this, and what to do if the stream path can't see the failure report.

